    "tail_excerpt": "\\Rightarrow a = 50^\\circ\n$$\n\nSo:\n\n$$\n\\angle BAD = 50^\\circ\n$$\n\nThen:\n\n$$\n\\angle BAC = \\angle BAD + \\angle CAD = 50^\\circ + b\n$$\n\nFrom equation (3):\n\n$$\n\\angle ADC = 180^\\circ - 2b = 2y \\Rightarrow 2b = 180^\\circ - 2y \\Rightarrow b = 90^\\circ - y\n$$\n\nSo:\n\n$$\n\\angle BAC = 50^\\circ + (90^\\circ - y) = 140^\\circ - y\n$$\n\nFrom equation (1):\n\n$$\nx + y = 140^\\circ \\Rightarrow x = 140^\\circ - y\n$$\n\nSo:\n\n$$\n\\angle BAC = x = 140^\\circ - y\n$$\n\nNow, from equation (4):\n\n$$\n\\angle ADB = 80^\\circ\n$$\n\nFrom equation (2):\n\n$$\n\\angle ADB = 180^\\circ - 2a = 80^\\circ \\Rightarrow a = 50^\\circ\n$$\n\nSo:\n\n$$\n\\angle BAD = 50^\\circ\n$$\n\nThen:\n\n$$\n\\angle BAC = \\angle BAD + \\angle CAD = 50^\\circ + b\n$$\n\nFrom equation (3):\n\n$$\n\\angle ADC = 180^\\circ - 2b = 2y \\Rightarrow 2b = 180^\\circ - 2y \\Rightarrow b = 90^\\circ - y\n$$\n\nSo:\n\n$$\n\\angle BAC = 50^\\circ + (90^\\circ - y) = 140^\\circ - y\n$$\n\nFrom equation (1):\n\n$$\nx + y = 1",
    "baseline_tail": "0^\\circ - 90^\\circ \\\\\nx = 50^\\circ\n$$\n\nNow substitute $ x = 50^\\circ $ into equation (3):\n\n$$\n50^\\circ + y = 90^\\circ \\Rightarrow y = 40^\\circ\n$$\n\n---\n\n### Step 6: Find $ \\angle BAC $\n\n$$\n\\angle BAC = x + y = 50^\\circ + 40^\\circ = \\boxed{90^\\circ}\n$$\n\n---\n\n### \u2705 Final Answer:\n\n$$\n\\boxed{90^\\circ}\n$$",
